      "Mathematical/algorithmic property: gcd should return the mathematically correct greatest common divisor even when inputs include INT_MIN, and it should not be affected by overflow/undefined behavior in the internal abs/negation step.",
      "Concrete values demonstrating violation (from issue reproducer): a = np.int32(np.iinfo(np.int32).min); q = -(a // 4); expected np.gcd(a, q * 3) = 536870912, but it produces -536870912 (sign flipped).",
      "Concrete failing assertion (from issue reproducer test log): np.gcd(a, q*3) with a=np.int32(-2147483648) and q=np.int32(536870912) gives ACTUAL np.int32(-536870912) vs DESIRED np.int32(536870912).",
      "Additional test cases added to cover ordering: assert_equal(np.gcd(q*3, a), q) and assert_equal(np.gcd(-q*3, a), q), as well as np.gcd(a, -q*3), all tied to handling abs(INT_MIN) without overflow/undefined behavior.",
      "Source of numerical failure: expression a < 0 ? -a : a is undefined behavior when a = INT_MIN on s390x; fix casts to unsigned to avoid overflow when negating minimum signed value."
